craftkit is licensed under either of

    MIT, at your option, or
    Apache License, Version 2.0

at your option.

This file states the choice rather than reproducing the two texts. A licence is
a legal instrument, and a paraphrase of one is not a licence: shipping a
transcription that differs from the canonical text in a single word would be
worse than shipping none. The authoritative texts are at

    MIT:         https://spdx.org/licenses/MIT.html
    Apache-2.0:  https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

and the SPDX expression recorded in every `Cargo.toml` in this workspace is

    license = "MIT OR Apache-2.0"

which is the machine-readable form of the choice above, and the form that
`cargo` publishes, `cargo deny` checks and downstream consumers read.

When you copy this project, add the two licence files from those URLs to the
repository root. That is the one step in the copying instructions in README.md
that this scaffold cannot do for you.

See ATTRIBUTION.md for the provenance of every file and every dependency.